  "scope": "# Review \u2014 51e59bb53cac\nTask/source: approved canonical generator v2.0.0, SHA-256 `08b4b873024c61e19e2ca44712559069050ca1493b88d76ab19b8c1b72346d36`; rule hash `6efb83adf2b2`.\nNeed \u2192 repair: missing parametric support \u2192 built a proposed fixed-per-episode `swap_scope \u2208 {interior, exterior}` prototype.\nCanonical/default: `interior` is the exact existing Racket rule; approved generator, canonical ledger, and production API are unchanged.\nAlternate: `exterior` preserves frame/color-role reasoning and swaps the same two colors only strictly outside the frame rectangle.\nRacket evidence: seed 17 produced both settings with 2 demos + 4 distinct queries, 6 unique inputs each, 62 executions, and canonical parity 8/8.\nTeaching evidence: demonstrations alone uniquely select the episode setting against interior, exterior, global-swap, and identity rivals for all 8 retained queries.\nPublic boundary: visible-only challenge bytes, opaque SHA-256 names, and public-ID-sorted batch emission; hidden setting, seed, programs, setting map, and query answers stay private.\nChecks: focused prototype suite **6/6 passed**; portable selected-task suite **63/63 passed**.\nTest harness repair: portable root discovery plus whitespace-normalized Racket authority comparison; no semantic or source-authority change.\nTickets: one Racket-confirmed nearest-anchor counterexample retained; one accepted-partial public-ID tool request reproduced over 8 assets/4 exports.\nRemaining limit: bounded prototype/rival evidence only; no alternate-rule approval, production integration, or training admission.",
